[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186150413 :answer-field/choices 17592186150416] [:db/retract 17592186150413 :answer-field/choices 17592186150414] [:db/retract 17592186150413 :answer-field/choices 17592186150415] {:db/id 17592186152104 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fab8d7a2-8042-5e4e-8fd9-ae407a4d21d4" "question-c922cf86-366d-5b96-b6c8-e7d64dc90ff6" "question-33c6a696-2687-53cf-91b5-ae5c51099777" "question-2fa5b801-b137-5833-adf3-4b3d17f99da2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151914 :question/worked-solution "To compute the unit rate of miles per gallon of gas, we divide the number of miles, $15,$ by the number of gallons of gas, $\\dfrac{3}{4},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n15 \\div \\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15÷\\frac{3}{4} & =15\\times \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\times 4}{1\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{3} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit rate is $20$ miles per gallon of gas." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152105 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7" "question-71f0d135-eabe-57fb-ab96-cf20fb60fc0a" "question-70693bce-1563-5043-b145-f1732cc4b8df" "question-bde894c0-0f60-52a1-8f53-44362f2c04ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151915 :question/worked-solution "To find the number of tablespoons in $1$ gram of olive oil, we can compute the unit rate of tablespoons per gram olive oil. We do this by dividing the number of tablespoons, $\\dfrac{1}{3},$ by the number of grams, $4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\div 4\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}÷4 & =\\frac{1}{3}\\times \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\times 1}{3\\times 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is $\\dfrac{1}{12}$ of a tablespoon in $1$ gram of olive oil." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152106 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-06090a54-3bf7-5dce-b7f7-51954f025453" "question-6cccdce8-916f-545e-8523-5e2c1794424a" "question-37159145-3e5f-53f2-822d-4367df7cb7bc" "question-6aea863a-357f-52de-8ad7-b9c9c32993ae"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151916 :question/worked-solution "To find the number of miles that Martha can swim in $1$ hour, we can compute the unit rate of miles per hour. We do this by dividing the number of miles, $\\dfrac{3}{4},$ by the number of hours, $\\dfrac{2}{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4} \\div \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by another fraction is equivalent to multiplying the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}÷\\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 3}{4\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{9}{8} = 1 \\, \\textrm{R} 1 = 1 \\, \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Martha can swim $1 \\, \\dfrac{1}{8}$ miles in $1$ hour." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-fab8d7a2-8042-5e4e-8fd9-ae407a4d21d4" :question/id #uuid "fab8d7a2-8042-5e4e-8fd9-ae407a4d21d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-71430" :question/problem "Suzie takes $\\frac{2}{3}$ hours to read $22$ pages of a certain book. How many pages can she read in $1$ hour?" :question/worked-solution "To find the number of pages Suzie can read in $1$ hour, we compute the unit rate of pages per hour. We do this by dividing the number of pages Suzie reads, $22,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{2}{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n22÷\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}22÷\\frac{2}{3} & =22\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{22}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{22\\times 3}{1\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{66}{2} \\\\  & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Suzie can read $33$ pages in $1$ hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2744fc75-9aee-5472-b571-e924eb38f9e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2744fc75-9aee-5472-b571-e924eb38f9e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "2744fc75-9aee-5472-b571-e924eb38f9e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95fb0629-d415-573c-9722-1d179bf8863b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7331676a-b6b0-50c8-abb5-bc1399ef4d38" "answer-b1c7732a-c197-5e0d-8737-34107092414f" "answer-72410a5d-4ed2-589c-9a96-915c6691fadf" "answer-95fb0629-d415-573c-9722-1d179bf8863b" "answer-00dc0803-4289-5d10-9911-65583cfc3728"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7331676a-b6b0-50c8-abb5-bc1399ef4d38" :answer/id #uuid "7331676a-b6b0-50c8-abb5-bc1399ef4d38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$30$ pages" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1c7732a-c197-5e0d-8737-34107092414f" :answer/id #uuid "b1c7732a-c197-5e0d-8737-34107092414f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$31\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ pages" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72410a5d-4ed2-589c-9a96-915c6691fadf" :answer/id #uuid "72410a5d-4ed2-589c-9a96-915c6691fadf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$32\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ pages" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95fb0629-d415-573c-9722-1d179bf8863b" :answer/id #uuid "95fb0629-d415-573c-9722-1d179bf8863b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$33$ pages" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00dc0803-4289-5d10-9911-65583cfc3728" :answer/id #uuid "00dc0803-4289-5d10-9911-65583cfc3728" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$38$ pages" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152646 :question/worked-solution "To compute the unit rate of feet per second, we divide the number of feet, $40,$ by the number of seconds, $\\frac{5}{6}$, as follows: \n\n$$\n40÷\\frac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}40÷\\frac{5}{6} & =40\\times \\frac{6}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{1}\\times \\frac{6}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{40\\times 6}{1\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{240}{5} \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $48$ feet per second." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186150383 :answer-field/correct 17592186150384 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-c922cf86-366d-5b96-b6c8-e7d64dc90ff6" :question/id #uuid "c922cf86-366d-5b96-b6c8-e7d64dc90ff6" :question/math-academy-id "q-67905" :question/problem "A leaking paddling pool loses $6$ liters of water in  $\\frac{2}{3}$ hours. How much water will it lose in $1$ hour?" :question/worked-solution "To find out how much water the pool will lose in $1$ hour, we can compute the unit rate of liters of water lost per hour. We do this by dividing  the number of liters, $6,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{2}{3}$, as follows:     \n\n$$\n6÷\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6÷\\frac{2}{3} & =6\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\times 3}{1\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{2} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the pool will lose $9$ liters of water in $1$ hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fd0af01a-73e4-519b-b081-ca37b5a21db0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fd0af01a-73e4-519b-b081-ca37b5a21db0" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd0af01a-73e4-519b-b081-ca37b5a21db0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2bd953d5-ff42-579c-acb2-def35c667d27" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f040a93-6f4b-5c58-ad19-03b03ef0421d" "answer-6754d3ae-b8b9-53e9-9b8a-a331a071d537" "answer-897c8d4f-efc3-5482-98f8-433b96884808" "answer-45dc3045-0571-5014-a74d-81cdca7770a0" "answer-2bd953d5-ff42-579c-acb2-def35c667d27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f040a93-6f4b-5c58-ad19-03b03ef0421d" :answer/id #uuid "0f040a93-6f4b-5c58-ad19-03b03ef0421d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$36$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6754d3ae-b8b9-53e9-9b8a-a331a071d537" :answer/id #uuid "6754d3ae-b8b9-53e9-9b8a-a331a071d537" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-897c8d4f-efc3-5482-98f8-433b96884808" :answer/id #uuid "897c8d4f-efc3-5482-98f8-433b96884808" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$7$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45dc3045-0571-5014-a74d-81cdca7770a0" :answer/id #uuid "45dc3045-0571-5014-a74d-81cdca7770a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bd953d5-ff42-579c-acb2-def35c667d27" :answer/id #uuid "2bd953d5-ff42-579c-acb2-def35c667d27" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ liters" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-33c6a696-2687-53cf-91b5-ae5c51099777" :question/id #uuid "33c6a696-2687-53cf-91b5-ae5c51099777" :question/math-academy-id "q-67896" :question/problem "At a fair, a carousel makes $3$ revolutions in  $\\frac{3}{5}$ minutes. How many revolutions does it make in $1$ minute?" :question/worked-solution "To find out the number of revolutions the carousel makes in $1$ minute, we can compute the unit rate of revolutions per minute. We do this by dividing the number of revolutions, $3,$ by the number of minutes, $\\frac{3}{5}$, as follows:  \n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3÷\\frac{3}{5} & =3\\times \\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 5}{1\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the carousel makes  $5$ revolutions in $1$ minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b3b22992-4d44-561b-9f44-cf2d5dba8e93"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b3b22992-4d44-561b-9f44-cf2d5dba8e93" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3b22992-4d44-561b-9f44-cf2d5dba8e93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-791d18e1-4093-5dab-80b1-2cdeeec278b1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-24c31280-ecb5-58d8-bd23-e18274f8038d" "answer-23801a00-f920-5878-a54b-0e06f4704881" "answer-4dd185bc-1d53-5d06-af55-d197af516931" "answer-791d18e1-4093-5dab-80b1-2cdeeec278b1" "answer-d14f5c60-8845-5e03-9980-e5ba4292d37b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24c31280-ecb5-58d8-bd23-e18274f8038d" :answer/id #uuid "24c31280-ecb5-58d8-bd23-e18274f8038d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23801a00-f920-5878-a54b-0e06f4704881" :answer/id #uuid "23801a00-f920-5878-a54b-0e06f4704881" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dd185bc-1d53-5d06-af55-d197af516931" :answer/id #uuid "4dd185bc-1d53-5d06-af55-d197af516931" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-791d18e1-4093-5dab-80b1-2cdeeec278b1" :answer/id #uuid "791d18e1-4093-5dab-80b1-2cdeeec278b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d14f5c60-8845-5e03-9980-e5ba4292d37b" :answer/id #uuid "d14f5c60-8845-5e03-9980-e5ba4292d37b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2fa5b801-b137-5833-adf3-4b3d17f99da2" :question/id #uuid "2fa5b801-b137-5833-adf3-4b3d17f99da2" :question/math-academy-id "q-169441" :question/problem "Owen takes $\\frac{4}{5}$ hours to do $24$ math exercises. How many exercises can he do in $1$ hour?" :question/worked-solution "To find the number of exercises Owen can do in $1$ hour, we compute the unit rate of exercises per hour. We do this by dividing the number of exercises Owen does, $24,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{4}{5},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n24÷\\frac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24÷\\frac{4}{5} & =24\\times \\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\times 5}{1\\times 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{4} \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Owen can do $30$ exercises in $1$ hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c50e92a2-cf53-5b22-b046-a98e26f50b91"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c50e92a2-cf53-5b22-b046-a98e26f50b91" :answer-field/id #uuid "c50e92a2-cf53-5b22-b046-a98e26f50b91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-670bc25b-0858-5ec5-b504-a4960a721849" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3d67f7b2-d4a3-5793-a2e5-0a9c8f9fd22e" "answer-670bc25b-0858-5ec5-b504-a4960a721849" "answer-9a470ff6-451e-5701-ab44-7dc1b2916a7c" "answer-8e517433-966a-5535-be1e-691cffcfef43" "answer-0d089f51-d83a-525c-987a-61fa02546ef1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d67f7b2-d4a3-5793-a2e5-0a9c8f9fd22e" :answer/id #uuid "3d67f7b2-d4a3-5793-a2e5-0a9c8f9fd22e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$27$ exercises" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-670bc25b-0858-5ec5-b504-a4960a721849" :answer/id #uuid "670bc25b-0858-5ec5-b504-a4960a721849" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$30$ exercises" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a470ff6-451e-5701-ab44-7dc1b2916a7c" :answer/id #uuid "9a470ff6-451e-5701-ab44-7dc1b2916a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$36$ exercises" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e517433-966a-5535-be1e-691cffcfef43" :answer/id #uuid "8e517433-966a-5535-be1e-691cffcfef43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{48}{5}$ exercises" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d089f51-d83a-525c-987a-61fa02546ef1" :answer/id #uuid "0d089f51-d83a-525c-987a-61fa02546ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{96}{5}$ exercises" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7" :question/id #uuid "8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-67843" :question/problem "A plane can travel $\\frac{3}{5}$ of a mile in $6$ seconds.  What is the unit rate of miles traveled per second?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the unit rate of miles per second, we divide the number of miles, $\\frac{3}{5},$ by the number of seconds, $6$, as follows:    \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}÷6\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}÷6 & =\\frac{3}{5}÷\\frac{6}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 2\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}\\times 1}{5\\times 2\\times \\cancel{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{1}{10}$ miles per second." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cde096b2-00d6-5b15-9126-741eaff0be29"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cde096b2-00d6-5b15-9126-741eaff0be29" :answer-field/id #uuid "cde096b2-00d6-5b15-9126-741eaff0be29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4fe3b194-43a2-5bcb-be96-d93b17b67cb8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4fe3b194-43a2-5bcb-be96-d93b17b67cb8" "answer-56c3a097-3da8-592f-839d-534722217b99" "answer-74859d4c-493a-53d5-b8ba-de3078dd8c92" "answer-e4b5b4be-4671-5f9e-9df6-8769608166bc" "answer-3ac93665-3485-5b87-afe8-8a6c218d990f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fe3b194-43a2-5bcb-be96-d93b17b67cb8" :answer/id #uuid "4fe3b194-43a2-5bcb-be96-d93b17b67cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{10}$ miles per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56c3a097-3da8-592f-839d-534722217b99" :answer/id #uuid "56c3a097-3da8-592f-839d-534722217b99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{12}$ miles per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74859d4c-493a-53d5-b8ba-de3078dd8c92" :answer/id #uuid "74859d4c-493a-53d5-b8ba-de3078dd8c92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{10}$ miles per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4b5b4be-4671-5f9e-9df6-8769608166bc" :answer/id #uuid "e4b5b4be-4671-5f9e-9df6-8769608166bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{5}{12}$ miles per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ac93665-3485-5b87-afe8-8a6c218d990f" :answer/id #uuid "3ac93665-3485-5b87-afe8-8a6c218d990f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{7}{10}$ miles per second" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-71f0d135-eabe-57fb-ab96-cf20fb60fc0a" :question/id #uuid "71f0d135-eabe-57fb-ab96-cf20fb60fc0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-67840" :question/problem "Johnny walked $\\frac{3}{8}$ of a mile in  $7$ minutes, keeping an even pace. How many miles did he walk in $1$ minute?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the number of miles Johnny  walked in $1$ minute, we can compute the unit rate of miles per minute. We do this by dividing the number of miles, $\\frac{3}{8},$ by the number of minute, as follows:   \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷7\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}÷7 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\times \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{8\\times 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{56}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, Johnny walked  $\\frac{3}{56}$ miles in $1$ minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a1b78218-0d64-5b00-9db3-4a0b69af469e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1b78218-0d64-5b00-9db3-4a0b69af469e" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1b78218-0d64-5b00-9db3-4a0b69af469e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2a8ec316-eac3-5582-ac9e-9d0ecabb5dd5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60efeb69-2291-5ab8-97b8-0921d4ea912c" "answer-ab7954bb-6098-5d17-87fa-f7398cad0ac1" "answer-2a8ec316-eac3-5582-ac9e-9d0ecabb5dd5" "answer-5454a88a-d451-5112-aaba-edf60456ae48" "answer-8a15ef33-1e8c-55f7-81a5-4f5dc6a79003"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60efeb69-2291-5ab8-97b8-0921d4ea912c" :answer/id #uuid "60efeb69-2291-5ab8-97b8-0921d4ea912c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab7954bb-6098-5d17-87fa-f7398cad0ac1" :answer/id #uuid "ab7954bb-6098-5d17-87fa-f7398cad0ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a8ec316-eac3-5582-ac9e-9d0ecabb5dd5" :answer/id #uuid "2a8ec316-eac3-5582-ac9e-9d0ecabb5dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{56}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5454a88a-d451-5112-aaba-edf60456ae48" :answer/id #uuid "5454a88a-d451-5112-aaba-edf60456ae48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{49}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a15ef33-1e8c-55f7-81a5-4f5dc6a79003" :answer/id #uuid "8a15ef33-1e8c-55f7-81a5-4f5dc6a79003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{56}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-70693bce-1563-5043-b145-f1732cc4b8df" :question/id #uuid "70693bce-1563-5043-b145-f1732cc4b8df" :question/math-academy-id "q-67874" :question/problem "A race car covers $\\frac{4}{5}$ of a lap in  $2$ minutes.  What is the unit rate of laps covered per minute?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the unit rate of laps per minute, we divide the number of laps, $\\frac{4}{5},$ by the number of seconds, $2$, as follows:     \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}÷2\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}÷2 & =\\frac{4}{5}÷\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\times 1}{5\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\times 2}{2\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\times 2}{\\cancel{2}\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{2}{5}$ laps per minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-728455ea-fb60-53bd-a006-dfa511296e5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-728455ea-fb60-53bd-a006-dfa511296e5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "728455ea-fb60-53bd-a006-dfa511296e5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aec67466-3054-5dc0-beb6-55abf9092bc6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a01ebef-f9b5-5146-8ea2-b0be45e8fdd3" "answer-31a2c1e0-465b-5463-ada3-ebc481d00702" "answer-3b52d182-7e17-5949-be54-a233c9d261b3" "answer-aec67466-3054-5dc0-beb6-55abf9092bc6" "answer-c5f5b6f1-8864-5516-86ca-c909870e413c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a01ebef-f9b5-5146-8ea2-b0be45e8fdd3" :answer/id #uuid "9a01ebef-f9b5-5146-8ea2-b0be45e8fdd3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\frac{3}{5}$ laps per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31a2c1e0-465b-5463-ada3-ebc481d00702" :answer/id #uuid "31a2c1e0-465b-5463-ada3-ebc4