edge-point/questions "question-2fa5b801-b137-5833-adf3-4b3d17f99da2"] ["question-8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7" :question/id #uuid "8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7"] ["question-8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-67843"] ["question-8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7" :question/problem "A plane can travel $\\frac{3}{5}$ of a mile in $6$ seconds.  What is the unit rate of miles traveled per second?"] ["question-8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7" :question/worked-solution "To compute the unit rate of miles per second, we divide the number of miles, $\\frac{3}{5},$ by the number of seconds, $6$, as follows:    \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}÷6\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}÷6 & =\\frac{3}{5}÷\\frac{6}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{5\\times 2\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}\\times 1}{5\\times 2\\times \\cancel{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{1}{10}$ miles per second."] ["question-8c31a83a-d0fb-50d8-8958-8a93c295b8d7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-cde096b2-00d6-5b15-9126-741eaff0be29" :answer-field/id #uuid "cde096b2-00d6-5b15-9126-741eaff0be29"] ["answer-4fe3b194-43a2-5bcb-be96-d93b17b67cb8" :answer/id #uuid "4fe3b194-43a2-5bcb-be96-d93b17b67cb8"] ["answer-4fe3b194-43a2-5bcb-be96-d93b17b67cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4fe3b194-43a2-5bcb-be96-d93b17b67cb8" :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{10}$ miles per second"] ["answer-56c3a097-3da8-592f-839d-534722217b99" :answer/id #uuid "56c3a097-3da8-592f-839d-534722217b99"] ["answer-56c3a097-3da8-592f-839d-534722217b99" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-56c3a097-3da8-592f-839d-534722217b99" :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{12}$ miles per second"] ["answer-74859d4c