0a" :question/id #uuid "71f0d135-eabe-57fb-ab96-cf20fb60fc0a"] ["question-71f0d135-eabe-57fb-ab96-cf20fb60fc0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-67840"] ["question-71f0d135-eabe-57fb-ab96-cf20fb60fc0a" :question/problem "Johnny walked $\\frac{3}{8}$ of a mile in  $7$ minutes, keeping an even pace. How many miles did he walk in $1$ minute?"] ["question-71f0d135-eabe-57fb-ab96-cf20fb60fc0a" :question/worked-solution "To compute the number of miles Johnny  walked in $1$ minute, we can compute the unit rate of miles per minute. We do this by dividing the number of miles, $\\frac{3}{8},$ by the number of minute, as follows:   \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷7\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}÷7 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\times \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 1}{8\\times 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{56}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, Johnny walked  $\\frac{3}{56}$ miles in $1$ minute."] ["question-71f0d135-eabe-57fb-ab96-cf20fb60fc0a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-a1b78218-0d64-5b00-9db3-4a0b69af469e" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1b78218-0d64-5b00-9db3-4a0b69af469e"] ["answer-60efeb69-2291-5ab8-97b8-0921d4ea912c" :answer/id #uuid "60efeb69-2291-5ab8-97b8-0921d4ea912c"] ["answer-60efeb69-2291-5ab8-97b8-0921d4ea912c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-60efeb69-2291-5ab8-97b8-0921d4ea912c" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}"] ["answer-ab7954bb-6098-5d17-87fa-f7398cad0ac1" :answer/id #uuid "ab7954bb-6098-5d17-87fa-f7398cad0ac1"] ["answer-ab7954bb-6098-5d17-87fa-f7398cad0ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ab7954bb-6098-5d17-87fa-f7398cad0ac1" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}"] ["answer-2a8ec316-eac3-5582-ac9e-9d0ecabb5dd5" :answer/id #uuid "2a8ec316-eac3-5582-ac9e-9d0ecabb5dd5"] ["answer-2a8ec316-eac3-5582-ac9e-9d0ecabb5dd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2a8ec316-eac3-5582-ac9e-9d0ecabb5dd5" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{56}"] ["answer-5454