 per minute?"] ["question-70693bce-1563-5043-b145-f1732cc4b8df" :question/worked-solution "To compute the unit rate of laps per minute, we divide the number of laps, $\\frac{4}{5},$ by the number of seconds, $2$, as follows:     \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}÷2\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}÷2 & =\\frac{4}{5}÷\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\times 1}{5\\times 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\times 2}{2\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\times 2}{\\cancel{2}\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{2}{5}$ laps per minute."] ["question-70693bce-1563-5043-b145-f1732cc4b8df" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-728455ea-fb60-53bd-a006-dfa511296e5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "728455ea-fb60-53bd-a006-dfa511296e5c"] ["answer-9a01ebef-f9b5-5146-8ea2-b0be45e8fdd3" :answer/id #uuid "9a01ebef-f9b5-5146-8ea2-b0be45e8fdd3"] ["answer-9a01ebef-f9b5-5146-8ea2-b0be45e8fdd3" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-9a01ebef-f9b5-5146-8ea2-b0be45e8fdd3" :answer/value "$1\\frac{3}{5}$ laps per minute"] ["answer-31a2c1e0-465b-5463-ada3-ebc481d00702" :answer/id #uuid "31a2c1e0-465b-5463-ada3-ebc481d00702"] ["answer-31a2c1e0-465b-5463-ada3-ebc481d00702" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-31a2c1e0-465b-5463-ada3-ebc481d00702" :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{10}$ laps per minute"] ["answer-3b52d182-7e17-5949-be54-a233c9d261b3" :answer/id #uuid "3b52d182-7e17-5949-be54-a233c9d261b3"] ["answer-3b52d182-7e17-5949-be54-a233c9d261b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-3b52d182-7e17-5949-be54-a233c9d261b3" :answer/value "$\\frac{2}{10}$ laps per minute"] ["answer-aec67466-3054-5dc0-beb6-55abf9092bc6" :answer/id #uuid "aec67466-3054-5dc0-beb6-55abf9092bc6"] ["answer-aec67466-3054-5dc0-beb6-55abf9092bc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-ae