igned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{3}{10}$ gallons per minute."] [17592186152647 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186150389 :answer-field/correct 17592186150391] ["question-06090a54-3bf7-5dce-b7f7-51954f025453" :question/id #uuid "06090a54-3bf7-5dce-b7f7-51954f025453"] ["question-06090a54-3bf7-5dce-b7f7-51954f025453" :question/math-academy-id "q-71434"] ["question-06090a54-3bf7-5dce-b7f7-51954f025453" :question/problem "A container with $\\frac{3}{4}$ gallons of weed killer can spray $\\frac{7}{4}$ lawns. What is the unit rate of gallons per lawn?"] ["question-06090a54-3bf7-5dce-b7f7-51954f025453" :question/worked-solution "To compute the unit rate of gallons per lawn, we divide the number of gallons, $\\frac{3}{4},$ by the number of lawns, $\\frac{7}{4}$, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}÷\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by another fraction is equivalent to multiplying the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}÷\\frac{7}{4} & =\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 4}{4\\times 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times \\cancel{4}}{\\cancel{4}\\times 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit rate is $\\frac{3}{7}$ gallons per lawn."] ["question-06090a54-3bf7-5dce-b7f7-51954f025453" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-09020a00-7821-5c7f-a323-c2393071bde1" :answer-field/id #uuid "09020a00-7821-5c7f-a323-c2393071bde1"] ["answer-16a97f78-f4fe-5855-b81b-381b3a37c9e7" :answer/id #uuid "16a97f78-f4fe-5855-b81b-381b3a37c9e7"] ["answer-16a97f78-f4fe-5855-b81b-381b3a37c9e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-16a97f78-f4fe-5855-b81b-381b3a37c9e7" :answer/value "$3$ gallons per lawn"] ["answer-1005ee30-9311-5fb9-a232-e0178b92429a" :answer/id #uuid "1005ee30-9311-5fb9-a232-e0178b92429a"] ["answer-1005ee30-9311-5fb9-a232-e0178b92429a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-1005ee30-9311-5fb9-a232-e0178b92